            <ArticleTitle>Age-adjusted international prognostic index is a predictor of survival in gastric diffuse B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>247-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bjhh.2016.04.010</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1516-8484(16)30035-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The clinical course of gastric lymphoma is heterogeneous and clinical symptoms and some factors have been related to prognosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The present study aims to identify prognostic factors in gastric diffuse B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed and treated in different countries.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A consecutive series of gastric diffuse B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma patients diagnosed and treated in Brazil, Portugal and Italy, between February 2008 and December 2014 was evaluated.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Of 104 patients, 57 were female and the median age was 69 years (range: 28-88). The distribution of the age-adjusted international prognostic index was 12/95 (13%) high risk, 20/95 (21%) high-intermediate risk and 63/95 (66%) low/low-intermediate risk. Symptoms included abdominal pain (63/74), weight loss (57/73), dysphagia (37/72) and nausea/vomiting (37/72). Bulky disease was found in 24% of the cases, anemia in 33 of 76 patients and bleeding in 22 of 72 patients. The median follow-up time was 25 months (range: 1-77 months), with 1- and 5-year survival rates of 79% and 76%, respectively. The multivariate Cox Regression identified the age-adjusted international prognostic index as a predictor of death (hazard risk: 3.62; 95% confidence interval: 2.21-5.93; p-value &lt;0.0001).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This series identified the age-adjusted international prognostic index as predictive of mortality in patients treated with conventional immunochemotherapy.</AbstractText>
